cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Trustworthy Stock Intelligence"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Chien-Hsun Chang"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KageRyo/trustworthy-stock-intelligence"
url: "https://github.com/KageRyo/trustworthy-stock-intelligence"
license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "0.10.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
abstract: >-
  Research software for schema-first, human-in-the-loop stock drawdown-risk
  analysis with temporal validation, calibration, uncertainty, trust scores,
  warning explanations. Version 0.10.0 refreshes each market's pooled model
  daily from validated provider history stored in PostgreSQL, publishes it
  atomically with recoverable failure handling and audited TPEx close
  corrections, supervises the local services, and keeps host paths out of model
  provenance. The served model is unchanged. It is not externally validated
  research or investment advice.
keywords:
  - stock risk
  - trustworthy AI
  - calibration
  - uncertainty estimation
  - temporal validation
  - financial machine learning
